gredient or side dish. Other varieties of the genus Capsicum are categorized as chili peppers when they are cultivated for their pungency, including some varieties of Capsicum annuum."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-bell-peppers"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell_peppers"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Succotash","dish/succotash"]]],["Cali-Mex cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-california-latino-and-hispanic-influence",[["Celery Victor","dish/celery-victor"]]],["Cuisine of California","cuisine/cuisine-of-california",[["Celery Victor","dish/celery-victor"]]],["Wampanoag foodways","cuisine/wampanoag-foodways",[["Succotash","dish/succotash"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Celery","ingredient/celery"],["Romaine lettuce","ingredient/romaine-lettuce"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Edible salt","ingredient/edible-salt"],["Lima bean","ingredient/lima-bean"],["Sweet corn","ingredient/sweet-corn"],["Tomatoes","ingredient/tomatoes"],["Zea mays Saccharata Group","ingredient/zea-mays-saccharata-group"]]}]},"ingredient/chhena":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/chhena","n":"Chhena","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Chhena ଛେନ୍ନା in Odia  or chhana (Bengali: [tʃʰana]) ছানা in Bengali, is a kind of acid-set cheese originating in the Indian subcontinent that is made from water buffalo or cow milk by adding food acids such as lemon juice and calcium lactate instead of rennet and straining out the whey."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-chhena"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chhena"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Bangladeshi cuisine","cuisine/bangladeshi-cuisine",[["Chhanamukhi","dish/chhanamukhi"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Maida (flour)","ingredient/maida-flour"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]}]},"dish/hindoostane-coffee-house":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/hindoostane-coffee-house","n":"Hindoostane Coffee House","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["The Hindoostane Coffee House, opened at 34 George Street, London in 1810 as the Hindoostane Dinner and Hooka Smoking Club, was an Indian restaurant, and the first of its kind in the British Isles. It was founded by Sake Dean Mahomed, a former captain in the British East India Company's Bengal Army. It closed in 1833, when Mahomed became bankrupt."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-hindoostane-coffee-house"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hindoostane_Coffee_House"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Swasthi's Recipes","ref":"site/indianhealthyrecipes-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"indianhealthyrecipes.com","note":"Swasthi Shreekanth's long-running blog of everyday Indian home cooking from across the regions.","url":"https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/about/","suggested":true},{"name":"Hari Ghotra","ref":"site/harighotra-co-uk","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"harighotra.co.uk","note":"UK-based cook Hari Ghotra's recipe library and videos of home-style Indian dishes.","url":"https://www.harighotra.co.uk/indian-recipes","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Indian cuisine","links":[["Akuri","dish/akuri"],["Aloo paratha","dish/aloo-paratha"],["Amba (condiment)","dish/amba-condiment"],["Annapurna Cafe","dish/annapurna-cafe"],["Baingan bharta","dish/baingan-bharta"],["Bombay potato","dish/bombay-potato"],["Butter chicken","dish/butter-chicken"],["Chaat masala","dish/chaat-masala"],["Chai Pani","dish/chai-pani"],["Chicken Chettinad","dish/chicken-chettinad"],["Chutney Mary","dish/chutney-mary"],["Dahi va