ent/ilish","n":"Ilish","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The ilish (Tenualosa ilisha) (Bengali: ইলিশ, romanized: iliś), also known as the ilishi, hilsa, pulasa, hilsa herring or hilsa shad, is a species of fish related to the herring, in the family Clupeidae. It is a very popular and sought-after food in the Bengal region and area and is the national fish of Bangladesh. It is also the state fish of the Indian state of West Bengal."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-ilish"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ilish"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Bangladeshi cuisine","cuisine/bangladeshi-cuisine",[["Shorshe ilish","dish/shorshe-ilish"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Hilsa","ingredient/hilsa"],["Mustard","ingredient/mustard"],["Mustard (condiment)","ingredient/mustard-condiment"],["Mustard oil","ingredient/mustard-oil"],["Turmeric","ingredient/turmeric"]]}]},"dish/tempura":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/tempura","n":"Tempura","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Tempura is a Japanese dish that usually consists of seafood and vegetables that have been coated in a thin batter and deep-fried. Tempura originated in the 16th century, when Portuguese Jesuits brought the Western-style cooking method of coating foods with flour and frying, via Nanban trade."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tempura"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tempura"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Bivalvia","ingredient/bivalvia"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Flammulina filiformis","ingredient/flammulina-filiformis"],["Shiitake","ingredient/shiitake"],["Shrimp","ingredient/shrimp"],["Squid","ingredient/squid"],["Wheat flour","ingre